fc:FCC00282 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Odor"@en ;
    skos:definition "The first thing that can be done after photography is an aroma test. Smell the mushroom as it is. Then, briefly rub a mushroom cap and the stem and smell again. You can also cut the mushroom and immediately perform a smell test. Record these aromas (almond-like, bakery-like, like dark cacao chocolate, apricot-like, like frozen orange juice, “normal/common,” cucumber-like, anise-like, garlic-like, coal-tar-like, radish-like, cedar-like, bleach-like, spermatic, shrimp-like, maraschino-cherry-like, acrid, etc.). | Aroma and flavor [See dedicated section further down]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme fc:scheme ;
    skos:notation "FCC00282" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Aroma"@en ;
    skos:related fc:FCC00282-values ;
    skos:scopeNote "Part: Whole Fungus. Method: Aroma and Taste. Data type: odor."@en .

